        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "7b588f95-3629-5674-824e-580da6917be3",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: H. P. Lovecraft, Timothy Leary, August Derleth, Donald Wandrei\n- Organizations: Arkham House\n- Places: Sauk City, Wisconsin\n- Topics: horror fiction, psychedelic drugs, weird fiction, publishing\n\nFacts:\n- H. P. Lovecraft was an American author born on August 20, 1890, and he achieved posthumous fame through his influential works of horror fiction.\n- Timothy Leary was an American psychologist and writer born on October 22, 1920, and he became known for advocating the exploration of the therapeutic potential of psychedelic drugs under controlled conditions.\n- Arkham House was founded in Sauk City, Wisconsin, in 1939 by August Derleth and Donald Wandrei.\n- Arkham House is a publishing house specializing in weird fiction, and it was created to preserve the best fiction of H. P. Lovecraft in hardcover.\n- H. P. Lovecraft died on March 15, 1937.\n- Timothy Leary died on May 31, 1996.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
